# Ability system

## Ability model

- Abilities are `AbilityData` Resources under `scripts/abilities/`. They define **behavior and rules**, not combat stats.
- Units own an `Array[AbilityData]`. Attach via `UnitStats.abilities`; `Unit.setup` **duplicates** ability resources per instance.
- Core combat stats (`move_range`, `accuracy`, `damage`, HP, move/action budgets, …) live on **`Unit` / `UnitStats`**. Attack **range** and **distance falloff** live on the attack ability; abilities still read damage/accuracy from the unit.
- Prefer the name **ability** (not skill) in code, paths, and docs.

## Required AbilityData API

- Fields: `id` (`StringName`), `display_name`, `category` (`MOVE` | `ACTION` | `PASSIVE`), `cost_slot` (`MOVE` → `notify_moved`, `ACTION` → `notify_acted`, `NONE` for passives)
- Methods: `can_activate(unit, ctx)`, `get_target_tiles(unit, ctx)`, `is_valid_target(unit, target_pos, ctx)`, `build_execution(unit, target_pos, ctx) -> Dictionary` (`commit` / `present` / `complete` / `death_units`)
- Passives: `can_activate` is always false; implement `on_incoming_damage(unit, context)` and/or `on_turn_started(unit)` when needed. `Unit.modify_incoming_damage` dispatches to `PASSIVE` abilities; `Unit.notify_turn_started` dispatches `on_turn_started` to **all** abilities (passives and per-turn ACTION state).
- Use `AbilityContext` for system refs (`pathfinding`, `grid_system`, `turn_manager`, `battle_state`, `combat_system`). Abilities must not cache Node paths.
- Execution may include intent for presentation: `presentation` (`BattleEnums.Presentation`), plus `path` / `defender`. Leave `present` empty so `BattlePresenter` fills camera/tweens. Do not reference `CameraRig` from abilities.

## Dispatch

- Player targeting is **ability-first**: `BattleUI` lists non-passive abilities; the player selects one, then clicks a valid target. Highlights and tile clicks use only `_selected_ability`.
- AI still resolves by `category` + `can_activate` + `is_valid_target` (`Unit.resolve_ability`); first matching ability wins.
- Presentation (camera/tweens/move log) is owned by `BattlePresenter`; `BattleController` orchestrates; `ActionRunner` remains the execution pipeline.
- Hit/damage math stays in `CombatSystem`; attack presentation calls into it (same role pathfinding plays for move).
- Attack `attack_range` and `distance_penalty_per_tile` live on attack abilities (e.g. `SimpleAttackAbilityData`), passed into `CombatSystem`. Cover penalties stay global on `CombatSystem`.
- Warrior basic attack: `attack_range = 1` (adjacent including diagonal).
- Grid defaults (Chebyshev range, octile move cost): see `grid.mdc`.


## Adding a new ability

1. Subclass `AbilityData` (e.g. `SimpleMoveAbilityData`, `SimpleAttackAbilityData`, `LeapAbilityData`), unique `id`, set `category` / `cost_slot`.
2. Override the four methods; read damage/accuracy from `unit`; set attack `attack_range` / falloff on the ability.
3. Put an instance on the unit’s `abilities` array (via `UnitStats` / spawn setup).
4. Do not add parallel execute paths in the controller when category resolve already covers it.

Standard abilities:

- Walk: `SimpleMoveAbilityData` (`id = &"simple_move"`)
- Shoot: `SimpleAttackAbilityData` (`id = &"simple_attack"`)
- Warrior attack: `WarriorBasicAttackAbilityData` (`id = &"warrior_basic_attack"`) — stamina cost, extends simple attack; cannot target directional full cover
- Warrior reckless: `WarriorRecklessAttackAbilityData` (`id = &"warrior_reckless_attack"`) — free action (`CostSlot.NONE`), stamina cost, once per turn; enemy retaliates first then Warrior hits
- Warrior shield: `WarriorStaminaShieldAbilityData` (`id = &"warrior_stamina_shield"`) — passive soaks HP damage with stamina
- Warrior recharge: `WarriorStaminaRechargeAbilityData` (`id = &"warrior_stamina_recharge"`) — passive restores stamina on turn start
- `CostSlot.NONE`: free abilities (no move/action budget); `can_activate` still requires owning the turn
- `CombatSystem.commit_attack(..., require_action, require_own_turn)`: pass `require_action=false` for free-action swings; both false for interrupt retaliation
- `Unit.notify_turn_started` dispatches `on_turn_started` to **all** abilities (passives and per-turn ACTION state)
- Turn auto-end (`TurnManager._try_auto_finish`) stays open while **any** non-passive ability `can_activate` (wired via `keep_turn_open_check`)

## Out of scope reminders

- Cooldowns are future work; keep the AbilityData API above stable for them.
